; sayBasics.inix -- a live test of EdSharp, played by tidy after a build.
;
; Tidy plays every macro in scripts\tests when EdSharp is closed, a screen reader is running, and the macro, the program
; or the key file changed since its last pass. It opens the build just made, presses these keys, listens to the reader
; and checks what Windows shows. It only says things and opens and closes the Alternate Menu, so it changes nothing.
; Play it by hand with: scripts\runMacro, which plays every macro here when none is named.
; Written 17 November 2026, when runMacro with no macro named found none for EdSharp and stopped.

FileTask = macroScript
App = EdSharp
; Say Position says the column, or "Blank" in an empty document, so either passes (17 November 2026).

Name = The Say family speaks, and the Key Describer describes

[steps]
Say Position
Expect speech column | blank
Say Status
Expect speech wrap
Alternate Menu
Expect window Alternate Menu
Press Escape
Key Describer Toggle
Say Position
Expect speech position
Key Describer Toggle
